          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "They aren’t indestructible",
            "body": "<p>A waterproof layer is a thin sheet. Rubbing, toenails and the wrong wash cycle will eventually end one.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Breathable doesn’t mean dry inside",
            "body": "<p>Work hard enough and you’ll sweat faster than the layer can move it. It slows that down. It doesn’t stop it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Keep your toenails short",
            "body": "<p>The least glamorous advice on this site and one of the most useful. A long toenail inside a close-fitting sock is a hole waiting to happen, and a hole can’t be repaired.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i4": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Don’t leave them damp in a bag",
            "body": "<p>A wet sock left in a kit bag or a boot overnight is where odour starts, and prolonged damp does the knit no good either. Air dry them the same day.</p>"
          }
        }
